<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    MSVC-mangled PE imports get a prototype (`option msvcsig on|off`).

    Issue: GH Noelo-Lab/kuna#990. A 32-bit MSVC image calls C++ imports through
    its IAT. The demangled-signature pass read only defined symbols, so each
    import was named from its mangled name and had no prototype: a `__thiscall`
    call lost the `this` MSVC passes in ECX, and a callee with no declared
    arity took the pushes meant for the next call.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement (`kuna-analysis`
    `analyzers/demangle/kuna_msvcsig.rs` reads the declaration off the import
    name; the commit parks it by address under the stated convention's model
    and locks it onto the import symbol) feeding P4 prototype-source
    (`ActionDefaultParams` / `ActionDeindirect` at the IAT call).

    P0 assertion: `option msvcsig on|off` (on by default, gated on `cppsig`).

    The fixture `msvcsig_protos_i386.exe` is the issue's clean-room repro,
    assembled from `msvcsig_protos_i386.asm` (see the fixtures README). It
    imports from arr.dll, where `Arr` is a 4-byte class with a destructor:
      ?IsValid@Arr@@QAEHXZ               int Arr::IsValid()            __thiscall
      ??0Arr@@QAE@ABV0@@Z                Arr::Arr(Arr const &)         __thiscall
      ?Note@@YAXJ@Z                      void Note(long)               __cdecl
      ?MakeStack@@YA?AVArr@@V1@AAV1@1@Z  Arr MakeStack(Arr, Arr &, Arr &) __cdecl
    0x401000 is `int Check(Arr *a) { int v = a->IsValid(); Note(v); return v; }`
    and 0x401020 is `Arr Build(Arr &x, Arr &y) { return MakeStack(x, x, y); }`.

    Pass 1 (`option msvcsig off`) reproduces the BUG: `IsValid()` has no `this`,
    and the copy constructor takes MakeStack's arguments.
    Pass 2 (default) is the FIX: `Arr::IsValid(a0)` with `this` typed `Arr *`,
    the copy constructor takes its slot and its source, and MakeStack keeps its
    hidden return pointer, typed. The copy constructor's evidence (it is
    imported) is what proves MakeStack returns Arr through that pointer.
    MakeStack's by-value `Arr` has a size the name does not state, so the
    parameters after it are left open; they are not recovered here, because
    the slot's address is passed to the copy constructor, so the pushes above
    it stay stores before the call in both passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/msvcsig_protos_i386.exe</com>
  <com>option msvcsig off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x401000</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x401020</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/msvcsig_protos_i386.exe</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x401000</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x401020</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="MSVCSIG #1: off drops this from the __thiscall import call" min="1" max="1">v1 = IsValid\(\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MSVCSIG #2: off hands MakeStack's pushes to the copy constructor" min="1" max="1">Arr\(a2,a0,a2,a3\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MSVCSIG #3: on passes this to the __thiscall import" min="1" max="1">v1 = Arr::IsValid\(a0\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MSVCSIG #4: on types the caller's parameter as the class pointer" min="1" max="1">int4 sub_401000\(Arr \*a0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MSVCSIG #5: on gives the copy constructor its slot and its source" min="1" max="1">Arr::Arr\(\(Arr \*\)&amp;v1,a2\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MSVCSIG #6: the hidden return pointer is MakeStack's argument in both passes" min="2" max="2">MakeStack\(a1\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MSVCSIG #7: on types the hidden return pointer" min="1" max="1">Arr \* sub_401020\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MSVCSIG #8: the cdecl import keeps its argument in both passes" min="2" max="2">Note\(v1\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
